Source: motd-forge
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: motd-forge maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc (>= 1.77)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: motd-forge
Architecture: any
# Declared by hand: dpkg-shlibdeps would add "libc6 (>= 2.39)" because of two optional
# (weak) symbols, pidfd_spawnp and pidfd_getpid, that Rust's std only uses when present.
# The real requirement is glibc 2.34 (Debian 12 and newer); CI checks this.
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libpam-modules
Description: themed, data-driven message of the day
 Builds the login banner from /etc/update-motd.d with swappable themes,
 alert mode and cached slow modules (updates, failed units, weather).
 A single self-contained binary with no dependencies beyond libc; all
 themes are built in.
